    "description":" Windows . C++ client, Discord API(connections). C# Builder    1. Get instructions from user  2. Copies instruction to stub  3. The stub creates the final product!                       Features   . Command Line execution  . Admin Access  . Obfuscation . Screenshot Grab . Wallpaper change  . Process killer  . List all processes  . Play audio   . Screen viewer . Process injection - Windows Only  . Discord token stealer . Play Audio . Listen to audio . Get exact ip using geolocation api  . Change Wallpaper   . Webcam capture  . USB spread . File Manager . Antidebug feature  . Keylogger  . Browser history viewer and deleter in a user friendly listed format ! . Shutdown  . Restart      Attack stages - Windows 11   1. Target executes thw  client on his system which will requires for him to allow   admin privelages (Note: the file needs admin privs to execute for it to perform admin commands).  2. It will check for internet connection. If the internet connection is not available, the client will actively and sleep actively looking for a connection in constant while loop. This function stays active throughout the entirety of the program.   3. Upon execution,  The payload  will  display  an innocent looking  message. Note: This is customizable in the RAT builder. To avoid suspicion  , it is best recommended to display a message informing them that the file which they have downloaded is incompatible. The payload  by default drops  a similarly named exe which acts a decoy  in the recycle bin folder. This is an intented act of practice which i believe  will reduce the suspicion from the target.    4.  The payload  will then \"delete itself\" in the desktop directory and will then  spreads to all parts of the directories including Temp, System32 and  Documents.   5. The payload will drop a \"deletecheck.exe\" file in the temp directory which will monitor the status of the client . If  the payload has been deleted, it will silently decrypt the base 64 encoded  url and download the payload which will be stored in the temp directory. the cycle repeats again. Note: You can disable this to happen in the RAT builder.  6. Payload injects its memory address into a random  listed  target process eg. \"processhacker.exe\",\"chrome.exe\",\"explorer.exe\" to achieve persistance   7. It will add itself to startup with an innocent looking name like \"chromehelper.exe\". Note: This is  customizable in the rat builder.  8. The payload will utilize the file hide api to hide itself   9. Voila now the target has been fully comprised!  10. Antivirus and VMS  - The program will constantly check for any Virtual Machines . If one is found,  it will self destruct itself and remove all traces including any keylog .txt files.    ",
